(A similar parity relationship between the prices of American calls and puts)Tj
0 -1.21 TD
(doe not exist.  As we discussed in the previous section, an American call on a)Tj
T*
(non-dividend paying stock is equivalent to an identical European call because)Tj
T*
(the early exercise feature has no value.  However, an American put is worth)Tj
T*
(more than its European equivalent because the right to exercise the option)Tj
T*
(early is positively priced.  Therefore, the prices of an American call and put)Tj
T*
(cannot be equated with the price of the underlying stock and a bond because)Tj
T*
(this price difference is not taken into account.  This is also the case for)Tj
T*
(American options on dividend paying stocks because the value of the early)Tj
T*
(exercise feature is not the same for calls and puts.)Tj
